{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>He is Aharon and Moshe. He is Moshe and Aharon.</b> For since at the beginning of the mission it appears that Moshe is the principal one — for to him alone did HaShem appear in the bush — I would have said that Aharon is subordinate to him; therefore Scripture says: ״הוּא אַהֲרֹן וּמֹשֶׁה אֲשֶׁר אָמַר ה׳ לָהֶם הוֹצִיאוּ אֶת בְּנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל״ (Exodus 6:26), to tell you that Aharon has a share in the bringing out just as Moshe does; therefore he placed Aharon first. But regarding the matter of speaking to Pharaoh, it appears that Aharon is the principal one and Moshe subordinate to him, for Moshe was heavy of mouth and heavy of tongue; therefore it says ״הֵם הַמְדַבְּרִים אֶל פַּרְעֹה מֶלֶךְ מִצְרָיִם הוּא מֹשֶׁה וְאַהֲרֹן״ (Exodus 6:27) — he placed Moshe first, to tell you that even regarding the speaking to Pharaoh he is not subordinate to Aharon, but they are equal in everything." "Another matter: for we find that before this mission, Aharon had been sent to Israel to turn them back from their evil ways so that they would be worthy of leaving Egypt, and in that mission Aharon was the principal one. And concerning this, Moshe said ״שְׁלַח נָא בְּיַד תִּשְׁלָח״ (Exodus 4:13) — that is, by the hand of the one whom you are accustomed to send, as Rashi explained on that verse (Exodus 4:13). And concerning that mission it says ״הוּא אַהֲרֹן וּמֹשֶׁה אֲשֶׁר אָמַר ה׳ לָהֶם הוֹצִיאוּ״ etc. (Exodus 6:26), for in that mission Aharon was the principal one; therefore he placed him first. But in the mission of now, whose principal object is Pharaoh, surely Moshe is the principal one; therefore he placed him first and said ״הֵם הַמְדַבְּרִים אֶל פַּרְעֹה״ etc. ״הוּא מֹשֶׁה וְאַהֲרֹן״ (Exodus 6:27)."], :book :exodus, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:18:35.512022913Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}